==Old English==

===Etymology===
Germanic ''*falwo-, falwa-'', from {{proto|Indo-European|pel-|lang=ang}}.

Cognate with Old Saxon [[falu]] (Dutch [[vaal]]), Old High German [[falo]] (German [[fahl]]), Old Norse [[fǫlr]].  The common Germanic is cognate with Latin [[pallidus]], Ancient Greek [[πελιτνός]] and Armenian {{term|ալիք||wave, gray hair|tr=alik'|lang=hy}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/'fæalu/|lang=ang}}

